      "message": "Give the forge's git its own identity, and nothing of the operator's\n\nWriting a receipt onto a commit is writing a commit under refs/notes,\nand git wants to know who by. On a machine with a ~/.gitconfig that was\nwhoever happened to run the forge; on a machine without one, GitHub's\nrunners among them, the note was never written and the mirror's suite\nwent red on the change that introduced receipts. Every git the forge\nruns now carries its own author and committer, reads no global or system\nconfiguration, and never prompts. The queue's rebase already did this\nfor itself; now nothing the forge does depends on what the operator's\nown git is configured to do.\n\nChange-Id: Igitidentity0076hermetic\nSigned-off-by: Mandip Adhikari <92096340+mandipadk@users.noreply.github.com>",
